  "body": "Is canvas hit region dead or is it still expected to be implemented?\n\nIn any case, could this not be decoupled from canvas 2d? AFAICT the only connections are the currentpath and the current transform. If those 2 things were passed in instead of inferred then hitregions would be usable for WebGL as well (and possibly other things).\n\nI suppose in the worst case you can layer a canvas 2d over a webgl canvas. That still brings up the speed issue though from #1029 in which case you might want to be able to pass in a 4x4 matrix instead of the canvas 2d's 2x3 matrix.\n",
